Engineering Student Resources Career AIM Handshake Parker Dewey Blog Events Career Services Our goal in Career Services is to help our students gain the knowledge necessary to be successful in their future jobs and careers. We provide them with opportunities to enhance and develop career readiness skills and guide them in their job search. Tell us about your Internship Did you recently complete an internship, or do you have an upcoming internship?  If so, we want to hear about it!  Please complete the form above to share your information with us. Feel free to contact Career Services by emailing CareerServices@saumag.edu . Career Services is available to help review resumes, perform mock interviews, and answer any questions students may have. Networking Opportunities Job and Career Fairs – Job and Career fairs are held throughout the semester. These events provide our students with the ability to network and communicate with potential employers. On-Campus Interviews – Employers utilize our campus for interviews with our students. Career Services Events – The Career Services office and other departments on campus host career prep and skill development events throughout the year. These events are free to our students. On-Campus Employment We do not place students in jobs but offer a bridge between students and supervisors. Students can see On Campus job opportunities here and are encouraged to complete the Student Worker Data Sheet online so that supervisors can see their availability and skills. Student Worker Training Students are encouraged to complete Student Worker Training once they have a job on campus. Registration can be found here . Contact Us Contact Us Forms Student Worker Training Student Worker Data Sheet Student Worker Applications (Faculty/Staff Only) Recent Postings TurnUp Civics Intern State Farm Internship Distribution Designer Talent Management Specialist Process Operating Technician Engineering – Pricing & Supply Chain Intern Multimedia Journalist 